			<span class="eyebrow">Timing</span>
			<h2>How This Fits Into Your 1031 Clock</h2>
			<ExchangeTimeline />
			<p>
				After your building closes, you have <strong>45 days</strong> to identify replacement property and <strong>180 days</strong> to close on it. Those
				deadlines are firm, and a NNN purchase can take time to find, negotiate, and close. A DST often closes faster, which is why some owners identify one as a backup.
			</p>
			<p>
				The way to ease the pressure is to start before the sale closes. We bring in your NNN broker once contingencies are removed on your building,
				so offers can go out while escrow is still open, and we build a 30-day escrow extension option into our counter offers. Read the full
				process on our <a href="/1031-exchanges/">1031 exchange page</a>, or the article on
				<a href="/insights/1031-exchange-into-triple-net-properties/">exchanging into triple-net properties</a>.
